    "created_at": "2026-07-04T13:37:03Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-07-04T13:37:03Z",
    "body": "Thanks for the responses. I'll start opening implementation bugs.\r\n\r\n> I haven't had time to check in detail whether this has any unexpected semantic side effects, but the approach looks fine.\r\n\r\nThe `async_sequence<T>` machinery in Web IDL was largely based on the original semantics for `ReadableStream.from()`, so the behavior *should* be unchanged. Well, except for strings, but that's explained above and tested in https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/59594. (By the way, reviews welcome! 😉)",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
